# Forsaken Miner dies to Bot2's Lightning Bolt on turn 2. On turn 3 Bot1 casts its own Lightning Bolt at Bot2 (targeting an
# opponent is a crime, CR 700.13). The Miner, in the graveyard, triggers; when the trigger resolves Bot1 pays {B} (a Swamp
# that was already tapped for it) and the Miner returns to the battlefield (untapped, a new object) while the Bolt is
# still on the stack, which then resolves for 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Forsaken Miner
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Forsaken Miner.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Forsaken Miner)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Graveyard = Forsaken Miner
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
